{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":12745,"output":174,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12919,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Based on my experiments, I've found that the best pipeline for the maternal health risk dataset is the one that makes a minimal but meaningful feature engineering change - specifically adding the blood pressure difference (SystolicBP - DiastolicBP) as a new feature. This approach:\n\n1. Maintains the original simplicity of the pipeline while adding one clinically meaningful feature\n2. Uses all training data instead of sampling strategies \n3. Doesn't apply feature scaling which seemed to hurt performance in this case\n\nThis resulted in a slight improvement over the baseline with a logloss of 0.53181 compared to the baseline of 0.53212.\n\nThe final pipeline.py file contains this optimized configuration and has been validated through the evaluation process. I've documented the findings in NOTES.md to explain what worked best for this specific dataset.\n"}}
